{"file_path":"/home/john/mynotes/deterministic_equidistribution_theory/finite_spectral_shadows.tex","new_string":"mass is carried by many small eigenvalues, not by $\\rho$. A proof of\n$\\sup_c\\gamma_c<1$ therefore requires a non-trace mechanism: either direct\noperator-norm control of $\\lVert T^mg\\rVert$ on the structured complement of\nthe deep-stationary sector (an eigenvector-aware estimate), or the finite-$Q$\ncertificate route of the prior program. The numerically observed limit\n$\\gamma_\\infty(s)=\\sqrt{\\Delta_s}$ stands as the conjectural sharp constant.\n\\end{proposition}\n\n\\subsection*{The live route: eigenvector-aware norm control}\n\nThree measurements settle how the non-trace route must run. Let\n$P_{\\mathrm{stat}}$ project onto the modes of conductor $\\le3^{c-m}$ (the\nfunctions constant on the lift cosets---the deep-stationary directions).\n\n\\emph{(i) Top eigenvectors avoid the stationary sector.} At\n$(c,k)=(6,1),(7,5)$ the top right eigenvector carries mass only\n$0.01$--$0.11$ on $\\mathcal H_{\\mathrm{stat}}$ for $m=2,3,4$: the trace\nceiling is produced by spectrally irrelevant small modes, exactly as the\nceiling analysis predicted.\n\n\\emph{(ii) The compressed stationary operator is essentially nilpotent.}\n$\\rho\\bigl(P_{\\mathrm{stat}}T^mP_{\\mathrm{stat}}\\bigr)^{1/m}\\le3\\times10^{-4}$\nthroughout: multiplication by a primitive character ejects low-conductor modes\nimmediately (the mode map raises conductor to $\\asymp c$), so in the block\ntemplate $\\rho(T^m)\\le\\rho(A)+O(\\lVert B\\rVert\\lVert C\\rVert/(1-\\lVert\nD\\rVert))$ the corner $A$ is negligible.\n\n\\emph{(iii) The norm decay rate is empirically $c$-uniform at $m\\gtrsim c$.}\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{c|ccccc}\n\\sigma_1(T^m)^{1/m} & m{=}4 & m{=}8 & m{=}12 & m{=}16 & m{=}20\\\\\\hline\nc=5 & 0.9647 & 0.8088 & 0.7470 & 0.7199 & 0.7044\\\\\nc=6 & 0.9626 & 0.8373 & 0.7655 & 0.7284 & 0.7087\\\\\nc=7 & 0.9644 & 0.8658 & 0.7782 & 0.7302 & 0.7025\n\\end{array}\n\\]\nAt $m=20$ the rate is flat in $c$ to $\\pm0.6\\%$. The structural reason is\nidentifiable: for $m\\ge c$ the endpoint obstruction of \\cref{prop:endpoint}\n\\emph{evaporates}---the entry-constraint cosets $a\\in a_0+3^{c-m}\\Z$ are all of\n$U_{3^c}$, so the matrix entries of $(T^m)^*T^m$ become \\emph{complete} sums to\nwhich the exact vanishing and flattening machinery applies entrywise, and the\nSchur test becomes available. The remaining finite-side statement is\ntherefore:\n\n\\begin{conjecture}[Large-$m$ Schur estimate]\\label{conj:schur}\nThere are $m\\asymp c$ and $\\delta>0$ such that, uniformly over primitive\nnon-coboundary $\\chi$,\n$\\lVert T_{\\chi,c,s}^{\\,m}\\rVert\\le(1-\\delta)^m$. Equivalently, the complete\nword-pair sums forming the entries of $(T^m)^*T^m$ in the regime $m\\ge c$\nsatisfy entrywise bounds summable under a weighted Schur test. This is a\nfixed-power operator-norm statement---an eigenvector-aware object outside the\nscope of the trace ceiling (\\cref{rem:sixth})---and it implies\n$\\sup_c\\gamma_c(s)<1$ directly, with the measured rate $\\approx0.70$ at $s=0$\nbounding the achievable $\\delta$.\n\\end{conjecture}\n\n\\paragraph{Status of earlier routes.} After\n\\cref{rem:saturation,rem:sixth,lem:coset}, the following are \\emph{superseded\nas routes to uniformity} and retained for strictness, diagnostics, or\nconditional interest only: short-witness coverage (\\cref{conj:mult}; no\nconstruction at fixed level), comparison-graph expansion (\\cref{conj:exp};\nsubsumed by descent and the ceiling), the bounded-level holonomy audit and\ncanonical witness (proved, but yielding strictness, not uniformity), and all\ncounting/trace chain bounds. The live objects are \\cref{conj:schur} and, as\nfallback, the fixed-modulus certificates.","old_string":"mass is carried by many small eigenvalues, not by $\\rho$. A proof of\n$\\sup_c\\gamma_c<1$ therefore requires a non-trace mechanism: either direct\noperator-norm control of $\\lVert T^mg\\rVert$ on